From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "adnan.drina" <adnan.drina@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 08:38:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(kanban): the --skills preload records what it
 actually loaded

RHOAI3 v24 review (2026-09-29): a Kanban worker's required skills are preloaded
with --skills on every run, but the evidence of that preload was the requested
argv, and the native finalizer continues when one skill loads and another is
missing, disabled or times out. The native preload now records, for a Kanban
worker (HERMES_KANBAN_TASK and _RUN_ID set), one 'preload' row in the task's
execution ledger: status loaded / partial / failed / timeout / error /
no-result, the requested names, the missing ones, and for each skill that
ACTUALLY loaded its resolved SKILL.md, that file's sha256 and the digest of
the text folded into the prompt. A requested skill that did not load is never
listed as loaded. Best-effort; no sidecar, no second controller.
---
 agent/skill_commands.py                    |  31 +++--
 cli.py                                     |  45 ++++++++
 tests/agent/test_rhoai3_preload_receipt.py | 127 +++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 196 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 tests/agent/test_rhoai3_preload_receipt.py

